6. Copyleft obligations that need attention when distributing binaries
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Nothing linked into either binary is under the GPL.

Every LGPL-licensed OCaml library we link carries a linking exception, so none
of them imposes a relink obligation. The one obligation is:

- libgmp is shipped under LGPL-3.0-or-later. We bundle a copy of it in the
  package's lib/ directory rather than relying on one already present on the
  recipient's system, so section 4(d)(1) of that license does not apply and we
  instead convey GMP itself under the LGPL. Accordingly the package includes
  the LGPL-3.0 and GPL-3.0 texts (LICENSES/LGPL-3.0-or-later.txt and
  third-party-licenses/GPL-3.0-only.txt), this notice states that GMP is used
  and covered by them, and its source is offered below. Linking stays dynamic,
  so a recipient can substitute a modified, interface-compatible GMP.

  Written offer: the version of GMP shipped in a package is recorded in the
  bundled library itself. Source for every released version is archived at
  https://gmplib.org/download/gmp/. If you cannot obtain it there, request it
  at https://github.com/soteria-tools/soteria/issues and we will provide it.
  This offer is valid to anyone in possession of these binaries, for at least
  three years from the date the package was released.

